{
  "rule": 1,
  "title": "DOM text normalization: line endings and NUL (FORMA-182, design 4 lines 103-106, DR-9)",
  "contract": "N(s): each CRLF pair becomes one LF, each remaining CR becomes LF, each NUL becomes U+FFFD; every other code point is preserved. N applies per authored or bound value, after the permitted value-to-string conversion and before ordinary DOM text or attribute comparison, escaping or writing. It never applies to transport, declared props, state envelopes, keys as data, source strings or digests; the canonical text of a list key, written as data-forma-key, is N of a string key (keys.json, FORMA-181).",
  "consumers": [
    "crates/forma-ir/src/text.rs (normalized_chars) and crates/forma-ir/src/walker.rs tests: TEXT, DYN_TEXT, static and DYN_ATTR attributes, textarea, pre, URL guard",
    "packages/core/src/dom/__tests__/normalize-text.test.ts: normalizeDomText, createText, h() children and attributes, form-control text, adoption expectations, URL guard",
    "packages/core/e2e/normalization.spec.ts: the textarea and pre HTML parsed by the real engines and strictly adopted"
  ],
  "note": "Hand-enumerated finite vectors. Not a generator or campaign. A vector changed here fails whichever side no longer agrees. Lone surrogates are not representable in Rust strings: serde_json refuses the file, so the Rust reader panics rather than failing one vector; each side keeps its existing surrogate policy. HTML pre and listing share the textarea first-token rule (the `pre` section); a marker comment consumes that boundary, so a dynamic value behind <!--f:tN--> is never doubled.",
